Cell["\<\
We can use Kruskal-Wallis test to compare the medians of the two datasets (no \
outliers):

- The null hypothesis (H0) is that the median temperature is equal across the \
north and south groups, or that the difference between the medians is zero.
- The alternative hypothesis (H1) is that the median temperature of the South \
group differs from the  median temperature of the North group.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.92736861101766*^9, 3.927368616990814*^9}, {
  3.927368677020197*^9, 3.927368887269379*^9}, {3.92770655433889*^9, 
  3.927706559156792*^9}, {3.9310813786146297`*^9, 
  3.9310813815224247`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"7749b85e-b7b1-8d45-9dc8-\
5acc435fe485"],

